  body: "# Child dependency increase savings and transitional scope\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\n\
    The captured dependency chapter distinguishes benefits affected by abolition of child dependency increases
    from unaffected categories, and retains savings and transitional conditions for specified earlier
    claims or paid entitlement.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nDMG 16003 and 16010 use the 5 and 6 April
    2003 boundary in different ways. They do not create an unrestricted new claim after abolition. The
    parent benefit, continuity, cessation, later decision changes and unaffected categories need separate
    review; no present-day availability of any listed benefit is inferred.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\
    \n- [DMG 16000, PDF page 9](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5eda569e86650c4abf424bc2/dmgch16.pdf#page=9)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 16: Dependency increases.\n- [DMG 16001, PDF page 9](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5eda569e86650c4abf424bc2/dmgch16.pdf#page=9)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 16: Dependency increases.\n- [DMG 16002, PDF page 9](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5eda569e86650c4abf424bc2/dmgch16.pdf#page=9)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 16: Dependency increases.\n- [DMG 16003, PDF page 10](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5eda569e86650c4abf424bc2/dmgch16.pdf#page=10)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 16: Dependency increases.\n- [DMG 16010, PDF page 10](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5eda569e86650c4abf424bc2/dmgch16.pdf#page=10)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 16: Dependency increases.\n- [DMG 16011, PDF page 10](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5eda569e86650c4abf424bc2/dmgch16.pdf#page=10)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 16: Dependency increases.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation
    of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review is required.
    Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring time are separate.\n\
    \nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, individual advice,
    an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter reading order, footnotes
    and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural evaluation pass is
    claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol3-ch16`: PDF SHA-256 `98d3f27a839795c416988c7a5770c403b8f046be78de244feaf612e4515ac3ed`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `7d8c71fa0ff5bbf0e45ab1044c34ebd8cb9bac48f582b20924e3ba78fd12fe5d`.\n"
